title Season G ninth rung — point decompression on edwards25519 in pure Rye
prompt Keep climbing the Rye-first crypto-parity wave Lindy-first crux-first; Rye prioritized, Glow on green-witnessed Rye; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop only at custody gates. baton prin recur.
think With scalar multiplication GREEN and sent (eighth rung, HEAD b0035dc0ea), the remaining non-gated arithmetic rung before Ed25519 verify is point decode — the inverse of the group law's compression. Non-gated: decoding a public encoding is arithmetic, no key and no signature.
think Read Zig's std.crypto.ecc.Edwards25519.fromBytes to confirm the standard division-free form x = (u*v)^((p-5)/8)*u with the +-sqrt(-1) root branch and the sign fix-up, then authored the same well-known RFC 8032 5.1.3 algorithm in my own Rye over fe25519's public API — clean-room from the public mathematics, not a copied line.
think Derived every constant myself so no borrowed literal enters the tree: d = -121665/121666 by field arithmetic, sqrt(-1) = 2^((p-1)/4) by a fixed exponent ladder, and both exponents by hand from p = 2^255-19 — (p-5)/8 = 2^252-3 = {fd, ff x30, 0f} and (p-1)/4 = 2^253-5 = {fb, ff x30, 1f}. Added an internal check that sqrt(-1) squared is -1 so a wrong exponent byte would fail loudly.
think Parity net three-anchored: the sqrt(-1)^2 = -1 identity, a compression round-trip (decode then compress returns the original bytes, using the GREEN compression as the independent oracle), and Zig's fromBytes matched byte-for-byte on the recovered affine coordinates over the base point and its multiples plus accept/reject verdict parity across 48 encodings. Guarded the spread with a SpreadTooNarrow assert so the verdict test cannot pass by trivially accepting or rejecting everything.
obs GREEN on the first metal pass — no build fix needed. The verdict spread genuinely exercised both branches (accepted and rejected both nonzero), and the recovered coordinates matched Zig exactly.
obs Matched Zig's fromBytes behavior deliberately rather than RFC's stricter x==0-with-sign rejection, since Zig is the byte-parity oracle this round; the whole-signature constant-time posture stays the same named Season horizon (the ladders here are data-independent over public data anyway).
obs tame_style bans clean; the new file lands in none of the ratchet lists. Composes entirely over fe25519's proven public API and the group law's public to_bytes — no new field math, no new std.crypto call. Honest scope held: no key, no signing, no network, no funds, no real device — no custody gate crossed.
